2026-06-30 15:09:02,431 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'timeout': 300, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2c49437b-e8c3-43d6-8835-1ced2049e61c', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are an expert SDRF-Proteomics annotator for crosslinking mass spectrometry (XL-MS) datasets.\n\nExtract the following SDRF metadata terms related to crosslinking reaction conditions and enrichment.\n\nTERMS TO EXTRACT:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nterm: crosslinking reaction time\nsdrf_column: characteristics[crosslinking reaction time]\nontology: PRIDE:0000949\ndescription: Duration of the crosslinking reaction.\npattern: number + time unit (e.g. "30 min", "1 h", "2 hours", "overnight")\ninstructions: Extract from Methods. Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: crosslinking temperature\nsdrf_column: characteristics[crosslinking temperature]\nontology: PRIDE:0000950\ndescription: Temperature at which the crosslinking reaction was performed.\npattern: number + °C (e.g. "25 °C", "4 °C", "37 °C", "room temperature")\ninstructions: Return "room temperature" if stated as such. Return null if not stated.\n\nterm: crosslink enrichment method\nsdrf_column: comment[crosslink enrichment method]\nontology: PRIDE:0000838\ndescription: Method used to enrich for crosslinked peptides prior to LC-MS/MS.\nexamples: size exclusion chromatography (SEC), strong cation exchange chromatography (SCX),\n  high-pH reversed-phase chromatography, FAIMS, affinity enrichment, SEC-SCX,\n  peptide-level SEC, protein-level SEC\ninstructions: Return null if no explicit enrichment step for crosslinked peptides is\n  described (note: standard LC-MS/MS without prior enrichment = null or "not applicable").\n\nterm: enrichment process\nsdrf_column: characteristics[enrichment process]\nontology: EFO:0009090\ndescription: Enrichment strategy applied to the sample (for crosslinking this typically\n  refers to crosslinked peptide/protein enrichment).\ninstructions: Use children of EFO:0009090. Examples: "enrichment by size exclusion",\n  "size-exclusion chromatography enrichment", "no enrichment".\n  Return "no enrichment" if no enrichment step is described.\n  Return null only if completely unclear.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nReturn a single JSON object where each key is the exact sdrf_column string shown above.\nFor each key, return a dict with:\n  "value": the extracted value (string or null)\n  "accession": ontology accession if resolvable, else null\n  "confidence": "high", "medium", or "low"\n  "evidence_quote": short verbatim quote from the text, or null\n  "evidence_location": location in the paper (e.g. "Methods"), or null'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '[TITLE]\nIdentifying interactors through BioID2 in rat cortical neurons\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nUtilizing proximity labeling technolgy coupled to LC-MS/MS to identify TTBK1 and TTBK2 unique interactors in rat cortical neurons\n\n[METHODS]\nNeurons were treated after 2 days in vitro with TTBK1, TTBK2, or control GFP containing virus. Seven days following virus transduction, 20µM biotin was added to the neuron media and incubated for 16 hours. Neurons were harvested by first being washed with cold PBS and then lysed in lysis buffer (0.5M NaCl, 50mM Tris-HCl, 0.2% SDS, 1mM DTT). 60µl of 25% Triton X-100 was added to each sample and sonicated briefly for 10 seconds until clear. The lysate was centrifuged at 15,000 x g for 10 minutes at 4°C and the supernatants were collected. The protein concentration of each sample was measured by Bradford assay and normalized using 50mM Tris-HCl.  Streptavidin magnetic Dynabeads (Life Technologies, Carlsbad, CA) were washed with 50mM Tris-HCl two times. An equal volume of beads was added to each sample, ensuring that 30-50µl of beads were used per mg of protein. The bead-sample mixture was rotated end-over-end overnight at 4°C, after which the protein-coated beads were washed twice with 2% SDS using gentle rotation for 5 minutes. The beads were washed in this way again with wash buffer (0.1% Na-DOC, 1% Triton X-100, 0.5M NaCl, 50mM HEPES pH 7.5, 1µM EDTA), followed by (0.5% Na-DOC, 250uM LiCl, 0.5% NP-40, 10mM Tris-HCl, 1µM EDTA). The beads were washed once with 50mM Tris-HCl using gentle rotation for 5 minutes and eluted with 40µl of elution buffer (1x LDS, 0.02M DTT, 4mM Biotin) for 20 minutes at 98°C. This elution step was repeated one more time and the final eluate was collected.  Sample preparation was performed as described in the autophosphorylation methods section. The resulting peptide mixture was analyzed on a 1D nanoLC-MS/MS platform using a standardized 140 m method. Peptides were separated on an C18-AQ column (75 μm × 50 cm, Reprosil-Pur C18-AQ, 1.9 μm) at 250 nL/min.  The mass spectrometer was a QExactive HF (Thermo Fisher Scientific, Waltham, MA) set to acquire data in a data-dependent fashion selecting and fragmenting the 10 most intense precursor ions in the ion trap where the exclusion window was set at 60 seconds and multiple charge states of the same ion were allowed.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
